---
/* What KoboldCpp does, in four short points. The details live in the wiki. */
---

<section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="features-title">
	<div class="wrap">
		<h2 id="features-title">What you can do</h2>
		<p class="section-lead">
			KoboldCpp supports hundreds of GGUF AI models. Everything runs locally on your computer, with an NVIDIA, AMD, Intel or Apple Silicon graphics chip, or on the CPU alone.
		</p>
		<ul class="features">
			<li>
				<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-pen"></use></svg>
				<h3>Chat and write</h3>
				<p>Ask the AI questions, roleplay chat, write stories and generate text adventures. Supports Tavern character card imports.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-image"></use></svg>
				<h3>Images</h3>
				<p>Make and edit pictures with Stable Diffusion, Flux, Qwen Image and other AI image generation models.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-music"></use></svg>
				<h3>Speech and music</h3>
				<p>Talk instead of typing, hear replies read aloud with voice cloning, and create songs and music from scratch.</p>
			</li>
			<li>
				<svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-plug"></use></svg>
				<h3>Connect other apps</h3>
				<p>SillyTavern and apps made for the OpenAI, Ollama or Anthropic APIs can connect and use KoboldCpp as their AI.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p class="section-more"><a href="/docs/#features">All features in the wiki</a></p>
	</div>
</section>
